# {DB_NAME}

PostgreSQL data product database, provisioned with a fixed role/schema
structure and deployed through **Bytebase** GitOps, run by **Jenkins**, with
one long-lived git branch per environment: **{BRANCH_MAP_SUMMARY}**.
Promotion between environments happens by merging one branch into the next
(e.g. `development` → `main`) — not by a single pipeline sequentially
rolling out to every environment.

- Environments: {ENV_LIST}
- Branch map: {BRANCH_MAP_SUMMARY}
- Owner role (Bytebase's migration credential): `{DB_NAME}`
- Human/app roles: `{DB_NAME}_readonly`, `{DB_NAME}_readwrite`, `{DB_NAME}_ops`
- Schemas: `bronze`, `silver`, `gold`, `audit` (read-only), `sandbox` (free-for-all), `extensions`, `remote` (postgres_fdw)

